{
    "background_story": "Zuri was a young mother-to-be who had always envisioned a natural, intervention-free birth. As her due date approached, she prepared herself with breathing exercises, meditation, and a birth plan. However, during labor, complications arose, and her obstetrician recommended an episiotomy to ensure a safe delivery. Although initially hesitant, Zuri trusted her doctor's expertise and agreed to the procedure. The episiotomy allowed for a swift and safe delivery of her baby boy, whom she named Kofi. As she held her newborn in her arms, Zuri felt a mix of emotions - relief, gratitude, and a hint of disappointment that her birth plan hadn't unfolded as expected. Nevertheless, she was grateful for the medical intervention that had ensured the well-being of both her and her baby.",
